    {
      "box": [
        87.10237884521484,
        179.96376037597656,
        414.5535583496094,
        193.6546630859375
      ],
      "text": "A__\nto describe what happened during the Battle of Worcester\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.46228790283203,
        195.08067321777344,
        478.4261779785156,
        234.32354736328125
      ],
      "text": "B__\nto give an account of the circumstances leading to Charles II’s escape\nC\nto provide details of the Parliamentarians’ political views\nD\nto compare Charles II’s beliefs with those of his father\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.54750061035156,
        244.7506561279297,
        496.8616638183594,
        292.9949951171875
      ],
      "text": "37\nWhy does the reviewer include examples of the fugitives’ behaviour in the third\nparagraph?\nA__\nto explain how close Charles II came to losing his life\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.4622573852539,
        294.420654296875,
        435.0802001953125,
        319.62640380859375
      ],
      "text": "B__\nto suggest that Charles II’s supporters were badly prepared\nC\nto illustrate how the events of the six weeks are brought to life\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.82217407226562,
        322.85491943359375,
        474.7441711425781,
        333.6635437011719
      ],
      "text": "D__\nto argue that certain aspects are not as well known as they should be\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.54747009277344,
        344.0906066894531,
        487.8816833496094,
        354.8992614746094
      ],
      "text": "38\nWhat point does the reviewer make about Charles II in the fourth paragraph?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.1023178100586,
        365.686279296875,
        387.485107421875,
        418.9663391113281
      ],
      "text": "A\nHechose to celebrate what was essentially a defeat.\nB\nHe misunderstood the motives of his opponents.\nC\nHe aimed to restore people’s faith in the monarchy.\nD\nHe was driven by a desire to be popular.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.54747009277344,
        429.3934326171875,
        474.92401123046875,
        440.2020568847656
      ],
      "text": "39\nWhat does the reviewer say about Charles Spencer in the fifth paragraph?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.1023178100586,
        449.54937744140625,
        378.0711364746094,
        463.24029541015625
      ],
      "text": "A__ His decision to write the book comes asa surprise.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.82217407226562,
        465.0262451171875,
        391.781005859375,
        475.83489990234375
      ],
      "text": "B_\nHe takes an unbiased approach to the subject matter.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.4622573852539,
        479.06341552734375,
        490.0771484375,
        506.0723876953125
      ],
      "text": "C_\nHis descriptions of events would be better if they included more detail.\nD ~ Hechooses language that is suitable for a twenty-first-century audience.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.187557220458984,
        514.6962890625,
        500.8929443359375,
        539.5420532226562
      ],
      "text": "40\nWhen the reviewer says the book ‘doesn’t quite hit the mark’, she is making the\npoint that\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        87.10236358642578,
        548.889404296875,
        500.03997802734375,
        629.161865234375
      ],
      "text": "A _\nit overlooks the impact of events on ordinary people.\nB _\nit lacks an analysis of prevalent views on monarchy.\nC __\nit omits any references to the deceit practised by Charles II during his time\nin hiding.\nD _\nit fails to address whether Charles II’s experiences had a lasting influence\non him.\n"
    },
